{{inh+|lad|la|ambō|ambōs|g=m-p}}. Old Spanish consistently had {{m|osp|amos}}, representing the inherited form, while {{m|roa-ole|ambos}} existed in neighbouring Old Leonese. Later, Latin influence probably helped {{m|lad|ambos}} spread into Ladino as well, where it displaced the form without /b/.

